  "provenance": {
    "pattern": "big beat's riff bass: a big, syncopated one-bar bass riff with rests, leaping and stabbing against the break, the part a Chemical Brothers or Prodigy track is hummed by",
    "knowledge": "public knowledge of the genre: the pattern as drummers, producers and tutorials commonly write it; no recording was sampled, transcribed from audio or mined",
    "note": "One bar of riff: root stabbed twice, a leap up a fourth and a fifth, back to the root, a rest before the bar line — short notes (holds a quarter of their spacing) so the rests talk. The riff of the style jumps an octave; the bass register refuses a recipe line wider than seven semitones on some keys, so the leap is a fifth. Under the break-over-a-four drums. The drive and distortion on it are the gap."
  }
